                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "e14e2b44-96aa-31ff-bb80-5a73a7c93575",
                        "entry_id": "ceac646b-c162-38e0-b620-b5aa6e7b9b07",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A flute-player; a piper, flautist."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "rare"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "565d0ef6-cf2d-4631-821b-aeee28ab7d2a",
                                "sense_id": "e14e2b44-96aa-31ff-bb80-5a73a7c93575",
                                "text": "When the Lacedaemonians went to battle a Tibicen played soft and soothing music to temper their courage."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "ca50fab8-3691-4130-acbd-8f90660d5efe",
                                "sense_id": "e14e2b44-96aa-31ff-bb80-5a73a7c93575",
                                "text": "But this man’s words are spirit itself, and burn their niche in Time, to last as long as that will. Take two of them: “Soldiers, forty centuries look down upon you!” and again, “Behold the sun of Austerlitz!” When you speak, speak thus to men; such words are deeds; and come not as from one who beateth the air to the pitchpipe of the tibicen Ciceronical, but as the bullet to its butt; speak swordpoints, that press between the joints and marrow."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "8db6a853-7827-4a08-a329-e2d6698dc5d5",
                                "sense_id": "e14e2b44-96aa-31ff-bb80-5a73a7c93575",
                                "text": "We have no archaeological evidence that we can with certainty attribute to original performances of Plautus and Terence. We can, however, learn a great deal by examining Greek and later Roman evidence, including artistic portrayals of singers, tibicines, and theatrical performances, and some surviving tibiae."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
